WEBVTT

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:15.910
--Mac! Mac! Mac! Mac! Mac! Mac...!
--Liu! Liu! Liu! Liu! Liu! Liu...!

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:17.450
Wh-What's this?

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.580
The one who Mac is staring at

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.880
is none other than "Gearless" Joe himself!

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:34.890
Wait, you know Mac?

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:37.560
Nope. Never met the guy in my life.

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:54.320
Under the guidance of Yuri who
was once called the King of Kings,

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:58.410
he defeated "Gearless" Joe
and made his vibrant debut!

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:01.540
Since then, he's continued to break
his own undefeated record

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:06.040
and climbed his way to the top as
the second Megalonia champion!

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:17.390
Placing first in the IMA ranking...

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:23.100
Belonging to Jimmy's Megalobox Gym,
and the King of Kings...

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:29.650
Edison Liu!

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:42.660
The new King of Kings versus
the ultimate challenger!

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:46.210
The match to decide who
will stand at the top

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:49.420
of the Megalo-boxing world
is about to begin!

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:55.300
Liu! Liu! Liu! Liu! Liu! Liu...!

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:59.680
Liu looks rather delicate when
he's lined up against Mac.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:04.440
Yes. Liu definitely has the
speed and technique,

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.190
but this is anyone's match right now.

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:13.030
Of course, Mac is going to win.
Right, Ms. Asamoto?

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:18.620
Hey, do you want a Mac T-shirt, too?

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:19.700
No, I'm fine--

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.830
No need to hold back. We've got plenty!

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:24.960
Would you like black or pink?

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:33.010
What were you up to, Yukiko?
The match is about to begin.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:34.220
Yes.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.180
Who do you think's gonna win?

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.270
Well, Liu, of course.

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:43.390
Then I get free ramen
for a year if that happens.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:47.400
Wha... What about you, Joe? Liu, right?

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.610
Yeah.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:01.490
He's...

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:25.930
MEGALOBOX 2

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:44.600
He's fast.

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:48.810
The champion can't get a hit in.

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:51.310
He might be keeping his guard up
against the challenger's first attack,

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:53.650
but his movement seem a bit stiff.

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:00.320
And the champ's down!

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:11.120
Mac! Mac! Mac! Mac! Mac! Mac!

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:02.530
One.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:04.240
Two.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:06.200
He's fine. He just lost his balance.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.200
Three.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.910
Four.

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:09.790
Five.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:11.120
Six.

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.340
Stop running away, champ!

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:24.930
Mac's overwhelming power
completely dominated over

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:28.680
the champ's speed and
technique in the first round.

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:31.850
Yes! Mac's the best!

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:35.310
Mac is facing off against the
champion equipped with the Gear

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:39.860
controlled by the latest
brain chip created by ROSCO.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:44.700
Meanwhile, it seems that Liu has
actually lightened up his Gear.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:48.240
Yes. He's using less parts to
expand his range of motion,

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:51.410
which will him allow him more
flexibility and a variety of attacks.

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:55.790
But at the same time,
his defense is definitely weaker.

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:59.050
You could say that this gives him
the advantage when he attacks,

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:00.840
but judging what we saw in this round,

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:03.180
this might be a
miscalculation in strategy.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:06.850
Everyone's got their eyes on
round two and it's about to begin!

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:13.810
Good job, Mac. Keep this up
and destroy him and his Gear!

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:14.810
Right.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:16.520
Thoughts, Liu?

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.860
Well... His punches are definitely heavy,
but they aren't that hard.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:22.240
I'll be able to manage.

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:25.160
We were right choosing this Gear for you.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:36.040
Liu's going to win this match.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:39.800
Liu was able to see through
Mac in that last round.

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:44.220
He's completely different
from five years ago.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:54.890
Liu's movements are a complete
180 from the last round!

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:56.980
This distance definitely gives
the champ an advantage.

00:06:56.980 --> 00:06:59.520
Mac's having a hard time making a move.

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:13.330
Mac's been sliced across his forehead!

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:28.470
And Mac goes down!

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:31.140
One.

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:35.890
This is rough! Liu's spot-on blow
to the left definitely left an impact!

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:33.850
Two.

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:36.480
Three.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:39.100
Wait, stand up! Stand up, Mac!

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:39.100
Four.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.310
Five.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:42.980
Six.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:45.570
Seven.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:48.110
Eight.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:50.740
Nine.

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:05.420
Why isn't he taking him down?

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:07.970
He's being careful about Mac Time.

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:09.010
Huh?

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:10.590
Or...

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.510
...he's waiting for it.

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:16.310
The moment to lure out the
beast hiding in the darkness.

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:23.900
This round definitely belonged to Liu.

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:30.450
But we all know Mac truly shines
when he's backed into a corner.

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:39.420
Mac! Mac! Mac! Mac! Mac! Mac...!

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:34.870
Liu is very aware of this.
That's probably why he held back.

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:39.420
Are we finally going to see
Mac Time in the next round?

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:41.750
You can do it, Daddy!

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:50.180
Everyone wants to see the guy who doesn't
give up come out victorious in the end!

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:51.180
Yes.

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:55.140
The unyielding hero who stands back up,
no matter how many times he goes down.

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:57.220
Mac's a true hero!

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:11.280
Holding back?

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:12.740
Come at me.

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:21.250
There it is! Mac Time has begun!

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.170
Mac goes down yet again!

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:30.340
One.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:34.510
Two.

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.600
His body's still dealing
with the blow to the left

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:37.220
Three.

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:38.220
he took when he first went down.

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:39.850
Four.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:40.600
His guard went down
without him realizing it.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:42.440
Five.

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:43.730
So Liu's right uppercut
was actually a feint?

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:45.020
Six.

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:47.570
Yeah. Mac's nothing more
than Liu's puppet now.

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:47.570
Seven.

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:48.780
Eight.

00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:52.240
Nine.

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:54.620
And Mac's back on his feet again!

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:03.330
We've seen Mac Time turn
the tables many times before,

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:06.000
but is it powerless against the champion?

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:09.210
Daddy!

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:08.190
The towel!

00:11:57.570 --> 00:12:01.870
With a TKO at 2:47 in the 3rd round...

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:04.950
The winner is Mac Rosario!

00:12:09.460 --> 00:12:11.920
Yahoo!

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:17.170
Who could have seen this coming?
The undefeated King of Kings has fallen

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:22.050
and we now have a new champion!

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:55.420
Let go of me, Bonjiri!

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:59.090
I've got an obligation to
tell the world the truth!

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:02.850
No! There's still a line
you shouldn't cross!

00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:21.160
If I only figured it out sooner...

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:22.950
No.

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:28.250
It's all right. Let's just
believe in Liu and wait.

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:30.250
I'll go buy us some drinks.

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:44.140
Once you step into that ring,

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:48.520
you either leave the winner
or the loser. That's it.

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:54.770
No matter what happens,
that is the fate of a fighter.

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:56.480
That's what I've always believed.

00:13:57.780 --> 00:14:02.910
The reason I took off my Gear
to fight you at Megalonia

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:05.570
is because I believed that was my fate.

00:14:06.580 --> 00:14:10.370
I should've been done after that match.

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:12.080
And yet...

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:16.460
I entrusted Liu with the dreams
I couldn't accomplish.

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:18.420
And because of that, Liu is...

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:21.130
It's not over yet.

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:28.220
I promised I'd fight Liu
after his match with Mac.

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:35.060
Sorry, but it appears that he might
have to break that promise.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:37.820
Liu's still fighting as we speak.

00:14:37.820 --> 00:14:40.530
It's too early to throw in the towel.

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:43.610
Stop holding onto hope that doesn't exist.

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:47.530
You know more than anyone
else what that can lead to.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:53.290
Five years ago, you had basically
put down your gloves,

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:56.460
so I should've stopped
your match against Liu.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:08.510
It's like I'm watching you
when you were younger, Yuri.

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:09.720
No.

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:15.560
He'll be able to go even
farther than I ever did.

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:41.210
The winner of the second
Megalonia is Edison Liu!

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:45.050
The dream that Yuri was not able
to see through in his prime

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:48.590
has now been realized
by his prized pupil, Liu!

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:58.230
It was because of you that I got to return
to the world of Megalo-boxing.

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:08.030
But... that's all over now.

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:16.660
Ouch, ouch. You're so strong, Miguel!

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:19.790
I'm not Miguel! I'm Mac!

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:20.880
I see.

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:22.840
It's Mac Time!

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:27.260
Oh, no! You got me!
There! Tickle, tickle, tickle...

00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:28.930
Hey, stop!

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:34.600
Daddy! No tickling!

00:16:31.350 --> 00:16:34.600
Okay, let's finish up the match.

00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:45.610
Now, Miguel. Don't be too mean to Daddy.

00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:47.190
Come have a seat and eat.

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:54.910
Hey! That's mine!

00:17:05.550 --> 00:17:07.880
It's okay. It'll be okay.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:14.600
Daddy's just really hungry
after his match.

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:16.810
Mommy!

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:22.980
There are times he seems
to revert back to a child

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:28.150
and becomes very obsessive over
toys and food, making Miguel cry.

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:32.320
Apparently, he doesn't
remember any of this.

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:33.450
After a little while,

00:17:33.450 --> 00:17:38.410
he goes back to being my husband
like nothing ever happened.

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:42.790
But... it seems to be getting worse.

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:49.880
Should I take him to the hospital?

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:54.600
His regular physicals and his exam
after the match were just fine.

00:17:54.600 --> 00:17:56.680
This might be due to stress.

00:17:58.180 --> 00:18:01.440
He pulls off quite a
performance in that ring,

00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:06.190
so I'm sure he must be physically
and mentally exhausted.

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:11.070
And I think it's your job to be there
to support him through this, Maya.

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:16.580
Let's keep an eye on him a bit longer.

00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:19.790
Mr. Sakuma, everyone is ready.

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:23.170
Have them wait a little longer.
This is very important.

00:18:23.170 --> 00:18:26.000
Oh, no. I can go now.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:28.960
I'm sorry to interrupt your busy schedule.

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:33.630
It's quite all right. I will always
be there for your family.

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:43.350
Please, come see me at any time
if anything else happens.

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:44.900
Thank you so much.

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:54.700
Now, then... How many minutes did we lose?

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:55.990
Let's get them back.

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:05.540
Because of Mac's victory, ROSCO's
popularity is up as well as our stock.

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:09.630
Our total market value is higher
than it's ever been before.

00:19:09.630 --> 00:19:11.210
Magnificent.

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:15.340
A man that suffered from total
paralysis became the champ.

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:17.220
No one could beat that kind of publicity.

00:19:17.220 --> 00:19:21.720
What's going on with the talks with
ROSCO to get BES on the market?

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:25.560
Currently, both companies
have put together a project team

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:27.560
to figure out how to bring down the cost

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:29.570
of getting the product
on the assembly line...

00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:32.900
Mac Time doesn't put him in the "zone."

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:35.900
It's abnormal behavior
from his brain chip.

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:42.870
If my hypothesis is correct,
BES has a severe flaw.

00:19:42.870 --> 00:19:45.210
Mac is in a dangerous state right now.

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:49.040
Wait. I'm not sure what you mean.

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:54.130
The data provided by ROSCO
hasn't shown any issues.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:56.680
Yeah, I took a look at that data, too.

00:19:56.680 --> 00:19:58.010
Then--

00:19:58.010 --> 00:20:02.770
A scientist's job is to look
into even the littlest of doubts.

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:12.110
I'm planning to release a thesis on
how the repeated use of Mac Time

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:15.150
is affecting his brain very soon.

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:20.740
I figured I'd let you know ahead of time.

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:23.290
Very well.

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:27.080
I may be out of line by saying this,

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:31.290
but you may only embarrass
yourself by doing that, Brother.

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:33.800
Hey, that's nothing.

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:37.550
I left my foolish pride back in that ring
when I stepped down from it.

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:43.850
Mac! Mac! Mac! Mac! Mac! Mac...!

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:43.850
You get blinded by ideals and lose sight
of the line you should never cross.

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:47.270
I used to be like that as well.

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:52.400
What about you, Yukiko?

00:20:57.070 --> 00:20:58.150
Ms. Asamoto.

00:20:58.150 --> 00:20:59.360
Yes, ma'am.

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:04.030
There's something I'd like you
to look into immediately.

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:08.710
I may have made a grave mistake.

00:21:35.890 --> 00:21:38.360
"Affordable Chinese Food Ichibanya"

00:21:38.490 --> 00:21:43.530
The typhoon continues to grow bigger
as it heads north across the ocean.

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:48.330
It is expected to be as big as
the devastating typhoon

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:48.660
Hey, that's my article!

00:21:48.330 --> 00:21:52.420
that wreaked havoc five years ago.

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:52.420
It's a great piece! Look!

00:21:52.420 --> 00:21:55.540
Residents living along the
coast are being asked to...

00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:02.800
Team Nowhere

00:22:26.030 --> 00:22:28.320
Mac's Time Has Come!!
